From 3fb6f34a97722ca34fec41b21d87164bf5663e5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:41:15 -0600
Subject: drbd: stop the start_resync timer of a dying device
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

From: Josef Bacik <josef@toxicpanda.com>

[ Upstream commit a439d3fe3ec2bfe0b4ccb77973ae97949bcf46ec ]

start_resync_timer gets armed for up to a second and nothing ever
deletes it, so drbd_destroy_device() can free the device with the timer
pending. Shut it down where request_timer is shut down.

Fixes: 370a43e7982d ("drbd: Work on the Ahead -> SyncSource transition")
Cc: Philipp Reisner <philipp.reisner@linbit.com>
Cc: Lars Ellenberg <lars.ellenberg@linbit.com>
Cc: "Christoph Böhmwalder" <christoph.boehmwalder@linbit.com>
Signed-off-by: Josef Bacik <josef@toxicpanda.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261028164415.1262013-13-axboe@kernel.dk
Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
[ sashal: kept the branch's existing del_timer_sync() context line for request_timer and added the start_resync_timer shutdown line after it unchanged. ]
Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
---
 drivers/block/drbd/drbd_main.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/block/drbd/drbd_main.c b/drivers/block/drbd/drbd_main.c
index b84d079d80b24..76af49ae899f9 100644
--- a/drivers/block/drbd/drbd_main.c
+++ b/drivers/block/drbd/drbd_main.c
@@ -2185,6 +2185,7 @@ void drbd_destroy_device(struct kref *kref)
 	struct drbd_peer_device *peer_device, *tmp_peer_device;
 
 	del_timer_sync(&device->request_timer);
+	timer_shutdown_sync(&device->start_resync_timer);
 
 	/* paranoia asserts */
 	D_ASSERT(device, device->open_cnt == 0);
-- 
2.53.0

